00:00:05.324 --> 00:00:06.140
NEAL MUELLER: Hi.

00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:08.379
I'm Neal Mueller, on the
geographic expansion team.

00:00:08.379 --> 00:00:09.920
We build the technical
infrastructure

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:12.350
that powers Google and
Google Cloud Platform.

00:00:12.350 --> 00:00:14.030
This includes new
regions, points

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:16.129
of presence, solar
and wind farms,

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:18.680
and terrestrial and
submarine cable networks.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.500
Today, I'm here to tell you
about our new amazing region

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:22.500
in Singapore.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:23.602
It just opened.

00:00:23.602 --> 00:00:25.310
The Singapore region
was built to service

00:00:25.310 --> 00:00:29.280
Southeast Asia, which includes
Vietnam, Thailand, Indonesia,

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:32.479
Philippines, Malaysia, and
of course, Singapore itself.

00:00:32.479 --> 00:00:34.550
This isn't our first
region in Asia.

00:00:34.550 --> 00:00:36.650
We also have Taiwan and Tokyo.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.750
Our global network
connects all of our regions

00:00:38.750 --> 00:00:41.660
together all over the world,
and our 100 points of presence

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:42.590
together.

00:00:42.590 --> 00:00:44.630
This global network
is the largest network

00:00:44.630 --> 00:00:47.190
of any public cloud provider.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:48.900
Now that I've told
you about the network,

00:00:48.900 --> 00:00:51.170
let's talk about the
Singapore region itself.

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:53.090
For the first time
ever, GCP users

00:00:53.090 --> 00:00:55.720
can process and store
data in Singapore.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.260
And as you can see
from this list,

00:00:57.260 --> 00:01:00.710
the services include
compute, big data, storage,

00:01:00.710 --> 00:01:02.000
and networking.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.665
You can find a whole lot more
detail at cloud.google.com

00:01:04.665 --> 00:01:07.760
/about/locations.

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:09.560
In short, the new
Singapore region

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.350
has everything that you
need to build and scale.

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:14.510
And now, let's hear a few
words from our local team

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:16.640
in Singapore to learn
what this new region means

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:20.162
for local customers.

00:01:20.162 --> 00:01:21.300
ANISH MALHOTRA: Hi.

00:01:21.300 --> 00:01:22.700
I'm Anish.

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:26.390
I help customers migrate to
Google Cloud in Southeast Asia.

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:29.090
You're seeing a huge
demand for GCP customers,

00:01:29.090 --> 00:01:33.300
like Carousel, Go-Jek, VPN,
and [? BWC, ?] to name a few.

00:01:33.300 --> 00:01:34.430
I love working with Go-Jek.

00:01:34.430 --> 00:01:37.280
We're using Google Cloud
infrastructure services

00:01:37.280 --> 00:01:40.580
to run their hyper-local
transport service in Indonesia.

00:01:40.580 --> 00:01:42.410
I also love working
with Carousel.

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:44.810
We're using BigQuery to
power the classified ad

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:48.700
